{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And it was evening and it was morning, a third day.</b> In these three days it mentioned evening and morning, yet there were no luminaries there that would necessitate evening and morning — for the setting of light is evening and its rising is morning. However, it mentioned evening and morning for all three, not with respect to the light but with respect to the sphere (galgal), which turns and revolves; for every part of the firmament, when it rises, it is for it morning, and when it sets, it is for it evening. But from the fourth day onward, when the luminaries were created, it mentioned evening and morning with respect to the light."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:24:59.525728258Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}